65.	 Headache
Headache is caused by traction, displacement, inflammation, vascular 
spasm or distension of the pain sensitive structures in the head or neck. 
Headaches that are new in onset and clearly different from any the patient 
has experienced previously are commonly a symptom of serious illness 
and therefore demand prompt evaluation. The precipitating factors, 
associated symptoms and clinical findings on examination, together with 
the results of appropriate investigations, can provide a guide to the cause 
of the headache. 
Causes 
Acute
yy
