('71','Psychogenic Seizures','6','Problems of the Newborn (Neonate)  .......................................','213','213-213','yy Recurrent tonic clonic-like seizures yy Attacks usually occur only when attention of other people can be attracted yy Patients hardly ever get injured, even when they fall (unlike in true seizures) yy Thrusting pelvic movements are common during “seizure” attacks yy Tongue biting, if it occurs is usually at the tip of the tongue instead of the sides as in true seizures yy May have urinary incontinence as in normal seizures',NULL,'yy Serum prolactin yy EEG','Treatment objectives yy To stop seizures yy To restore normalcy Non-pharmacological treatment yy Reassure parents, guardians etc. yy Counselling yy Psychotherapy Pharmacological treatment yy Anti-epileptic medicines do not appear to have any beneficial effect on frequency of attacks','Refer all acutely disturbed patients to a specialist. 71. Psychogenic Seizures Psychogenic seizures or pseudo seizures are non-epileptic seizures, which mimic epilepsy but actually have an underlying psychological cause. In patients with this form of disorder, there may be a history of physical, sexual or psychological abuse. The symptoms may be precipitated by stress and the signs are often variable and may include resistance to eye opening upon examination. The diagnosis requires a high level of suspicion since it is often difficult to separate from epileptic seizures and may, in fact co-exist with epilepsy. Symptoms yy Recurrent tonic clonic-like seizures yy Attacks usually occur only when attention of other people can be attracted yy Patients hardly ever get injured, even when they fall (unlike in true seizures) yy Thrusting pelvic movements are common during “seizure” attacks yy Tongue biting, if it occurs is usually at the tip of the tongue instead of the sides as in true seizures yy May have urinary incontinence as in normal seizures Investigations yy Serum prolactin yy EEG Treatment Treatment objectives yy To stop seizures yy To restore normalcy Non-pharmacological treatment yy Reassure parents, guardians etc. yy Counselling yy Psychotherapy Pharmacological treatment yy Anti-epileptic medicines do not appear to have any beneficial effect on frequency of attacks','— Psychogenic Seizures —
Chapter 10: Psychiatric Disorders
213
