92.	 Pruritus
Pruritus or itching is an unpleasant sensation on the skin that 
provokes the desire to rub or scratch the area. Itching can cause discomfort 
and frustration. In severe cases it can lead to disturbed sleep, anxiety 
and depression. Constant scratching to obtain relief can damage the skin 
and reduce its effectiveness as a major protective barrier. Treatment of 
pruritus must address the underlying condition. Diagnosis therefore 
needs to be made for effective treatment. 
Causes 
Localised pruritus (confined to a certain part of the body)
