 pain, yy Tenesmus yy Constipation Signs yy Anal ulcers or blisters yy Anal growth yy Tenderness on rectal examination yy Anal discharge or bleeding Treatment Treatment objectives yy To relive pain yy To treat for the major causes simultaneously Non-pharmacological treatment yy Keep lesions dry and clean Pharmacological treatment A. For anorectal discharge, treat for gonorrhea and chlamydia (See sections above) B. For anorectal ulcers or vesicles For 1st episode of vesicular lesions treat for herpes simplex virus yy Aciclovir, 200 mg, 4-6 hourly for 7 days (5 doses per day) Or yy Aciclovir, 400 mg, 8 hourly for 7 days Episodic treatment for recurrent HSV vesicular lesions to be started on first day of appearance of lesions yy Aciclovir, 400 mg, 8 hourly for 5 days Or yy Aciclovir, 800 mg, 12 hourly for 5 days Or yy Aciclovir, 800 mg, 8 hourly for 2 days And C. For Syphilis yy Benzathine Penicillin G, IM, 1.2 MU in each buttock (total dose 2.4 MU) stat. Or yy Procaine Penicillin Aqueous, IM (by deep injection), 1.2 MU daily for 10 days Or',NULL,'— STI-related Ano-rectal Related Syndromes  —
