('194','Xerophthalmia','6','Problems of the Newborn (Neonate)  .......................................','503','503-503','yy Poor night vision (in the early stages)','yy Dry conjunctiva yy Grey sclera yy Conjunctival folding (wrinkling) yy Keratomalacia (cloudy cornea, soft and easy ulceration)','yy Nil',NULL,NULL,'19
Chapter
503
Eye Disorders
193.	Neonatal Conjunctivitis  
(See section on ‘Neonatal Conjunctivitis’ under Neonatal Disorders) 
194.	Xerophthalmia 
This condition is common in children. It is associated with inadequate 
intake of foods that contain Vitamin A. It is a common cause of blindness 
in children. It is important to prevent this condition by examining the eyes 
of all sick and malnourished children. The diet of children should include 
foods that contain Vitamin A (dark green leafy vegetables e.g. nkontomire, 
yellow fruits and vegetables, palm oil, milk, eggs). 
Parents and other caregivers should be discouraged from putting 
any traditional preparations such as herbs, sea water, saliva, urine, etc. or 
drugs into the eye unless prescribed by a physician.
Causes 
yy
Vitamin A deficiency resulting from
yy
Protein calorie malnutrition
yy
Measles
yy
Malabsorption states
Symptoms
yy
Poor night vision (in the early stages) 
Signs
yy
Dry conjunctiva
yy
Grey sclera
yy
Conjunctival folding (wrinkling)
yy
Keratomalacia (cloudy cornea, soft and easy ulceration)
Investigations
yy
Nil'),
