220.	Oral Squamous Cell Carcinoma  
This condition presents as a non-healing ulcer of more than two weeks 
in the mouth. There may be a genetic predisposition but environmental 
causes have been identified. For an oral ulcer, 2 weeks observation for 
healing is usually adequate. If suspected to be due to an infection, an 
appropriate antimicrobial is given. 
