This is a degenerative articular cartilage disease of varied aetiology. It 
can affect all joints, but mostly the hips and knees. Important differentials 
include, rheumatoid arthritis and tuberculosis affecting the joints. 
Primary osteoarthritis is usually age-related (old age), whiles 
secondary osteoarthritis may be due to other causes. 
