242.	Necrotizing Fasciitis
It is a rapidly progressive inflammatory infection of the fascia with 
progressive destruction of the skin and subcutaneous tissue (also known 
as ‘flesh-eating’ disease).
It is a life threathening condition and if not properly managed may 
be fatal. It must be managed as an emergency. It is commoner in the 
immune-compromised state e.g. diabetes, HIV, malignancies.  
