('244','Tuberculosis in orthopaedics','6','Problems of the Newborn (Neonate)  .......................................','615','615-615','yy Pain especially at night yy Swelling yy Deformity yy Night sweats yy Low grade fever yy Chronic cough yy Weight loss','yy Swelling yy Tenderness yy Deformities yy Discharging sinuses yy Cold abscesses yy Muscle wasting','yy Chest X-Ray to rule out pulmonary TB yy X-ray of the suspected part yy Sputum/gastric washings for AFBs yy FBC, ESR yy MRI of suspected parts (if available) yy Bone and soft tissue biopsy for culture and histology yy Mantoux test','Treatment objectives yy Eradicate infection yy Prevent and correct deformity yy Prevent stiffness Non-pharmacological treatment yy Physiotherapy yy Splints/corsets/body jackets',NULL,'— Tuberculosis in orthopaedics —
Chapter 23: Trauma And Injuries
615
244.	Tuberculosis in orthopaedics
Tuberculosis can affect all bones and joints. The spine is affected in 
50% of all cases. It affects all ages but commoner in the extremes of age. 
May co-exist with pulmonary TB in some cases and also in HIV positive 
patients.
There may be a positive history of contact with a TB infected patient.
Causes 
yy
Mycobacterium tuberculosis 
yy
Mycobacterium africanum 
yy
Mycobacterium bovis
Symptoms
yy
Pain especially at night
yy
Swelling
yy
Deformity
yy
Night sweats
yy
Low grade fever
yy
Chronic cough
yy
Weight loss
Signs
yy
Swelling
yy
Tenderness 
yy
Deformities
yy
Discharging sinuses
yy
Cold abscesses
yy
Muscle wasting
Investigations
yy
Chest X-Ray to rule out pulmonary TB
yy
X-ray of the suspected part
yy
Sputum/gastric washings for AFBs
yy
FBC, ESR
yy
MRI of suspected parts (if available) 
yy
Bone and soft tissue biopsy for culture and histology
yy
Mantoux test 
Treatment 
Treatment objectives
yy
Eradicate infection
yy
Prevent and correct deformity
yy
Prevent stiffness
Non-pharmacological treatment
yy
Physiotherapy
yy
Splints/corsets/body jackets'),
